  "notes": "GAIA (Mialon et al., 2023; arXiv:2311.12983) is a General AI Assistant benchmark of 466 real-world, unambiguous questions that each require multi-step reasoning, web browsing, tool use, code execution, and multi-modal input handling. Questions are divided into three difficulty levels: Level 1 (at most 5 steps, 1 tool), Level 2 (5-10 steps, multiple tools), and Level 3 (long-horizon, near-perfect-assistant). The paper reports 146/245/75 per level.\n\nThe live HF dataset and leaderboard operate on a 165/301 validation/test split (53/86/26 and 93/159/49 per level). Evaluation is quasi-exact-match string accuracy via the official question_scorer in the HF Space, with light normalization for numbers, commas, and articles. The authors closed the validation leaderboard because contamination made it 'no longer informative', so the HF Space now only exposes TEST submissions — which is why OpenAI Deep Research's validation numbers appear in a separate 2025-02 blog entry rather than on the leaderboard.\n\nResults cover 2023-11 through 2026-04. Leaderboard rows come from the HF Space's test-split leaderboard grouped into six release eras (each entry's date is the latest submission in that window). The 2023-11 paper and the 2025-02 OpenAI announcement are separate blog/paper entries. There is no canonical GitHub repo for GAIA because the scorer and Gradio app live only in the HF Space, which is why `links.github` is null."
